/-- **ν and an optimal pose of `Johnson.ElongatedTriangularCupola.polyhedron` as one root**: when the representatives' systems have
exactly one root each, of scale `N`, the system `S` has exactly one root, of scale `N`, and at it
`matAt x 61`, `matAt x 52` and `(x 70, x 71)` are a weak fit of `Johnson.ElongatedTriangularCupola.polyhedron` scaled
by `N` through itself. -/
theorem johnsonElongatedTriangularCupola_pose_of_reps {N : ℝ} (h : PolynomialSystem.IsRootEq [Pose.JohnsonElongatedTriangularCupola.reps0] N) :
    PolynomialSystem.IsPoseRoot Johnson.ElongatedTriangularCupola.polyhedron Pose.JohnsonElongatedTriangularCupola.S N 61 52 70 := by
  rw [Pose.JohnsonElongatedTriangularCupola.S_eq]
  exact PolynomialSystem.ct_isPoseRoot h List.mem_cons_self Pose.JohnsonElongatedTriangularCupola.len_eq Pose.JohnsonElongatedTriangularCupola.reps_eq
    (Root.ParData.sqrt_spec (by decide +kernel)) Pose.JohnsonElongatedTriangularCupola.par_ok Pose.JohnsonElongatedTriangularCupola.zs_eq Pose.JohnsonElongatedTriangularCupola.weak_ok Pose.JohnsonElongatedTriangularCupola.poly_eq Pose.JohnsonElongatedTriangularCupola.ok

